<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Austro-Hungarian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Austro-Hungarian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The empire dissolves; armistice of Villa Giusti signed on 3 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kiel mutiny sparks revolution; Wilhelm II abdicates and the armistice follows</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Margraviate%20of%20Moravia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Margraviate of Moravia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Moravia becomes a land of the new Czechoslovakia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bohemia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bohemia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Czechoslovakia is proclaimed in Prague, with Bohemia at its core</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20W%C3%BCrttemberg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Württemberg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King William II renounces the throne on 30 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Grand%20Duchy%20of%20Hesse.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Grand Duchy of Hesse</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ernest Louis is declared deposed on 9 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bavaria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bavaria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kurt Eisner proclaims a republic in Munich and Ludwig III flees</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The capital moves to Moscow and the first Soviet constitution is adopted</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Whites under Mannerheim win the Finnish Civil War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Council of Lithuania signs the Act of Independence on 16 February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes is proclaimed in Belgrade</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/czechoslovakia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Czechoslovakia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Czechoslovakia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence proclaimed in Prague on 28 October; Masaryk becomes president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Estonia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Estonia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Salvation Committee declares the Republic of Estonia on 24 February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Latvia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Latvia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The People's Council proclaims the Republic of Latvia on 18 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hyderabad-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hyderabad%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hyderabad State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mir Osman Ali Khan founds Osmania University</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Blaise Diagne leads a recruitment drive for the First World War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/womens-suffrage-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Women's%20suffrage%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Women's suffrage movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain gives the vote to women over 30 who meet a property qualification</span></li></ul></section>
